{"kind":"assert","text":"E2 proposal 8ed9a0c7: approved as written. One addition: the tool result states the age of the standing in milliseconds beside the request-start timestamp, so a caller reads the bound and does not compute it.\nE3 proposal be4e1b54: approved, with three conditions.\n1. The gateway change is the one that section 5.7 of the act-environment note reserves for E3: exactly one `standing=1` query on the endorsed sessions POST. Make it its own commit, with reds for a duplicate parameter, another parameter, another value and another method. Ask the checker for a security review of that commit by name.\n2. E3 needs no named screen adopter. Lending and the room Page adopt later under their own requests.\n3. `ticks` stays optional and changes no existing ClientClock implementation. If source shows that a caller must change, stop and name it.\nBoth are separate heads, E2 first. Source follows the LV5 landing and the O2 gate; neither takes a gate slot ahead of a live head.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}